  "_note": "Arc Testnet (Circle), chainId 5042002. Verified live: eth_chainId=0x4cef52, reth v1.11.3, Malachite BFT, ~510ms blocks. Explorer https://testnet.arcscan.app, faucet https://faucet.circle.com (20 USDC per address / 2h, no account). UNLIKE Tempo, Arc PERMITS native value transfers, so EventDriven jobs may settle natively; the per-blueprint ERC20 settlement asset from #209 remains available. HAZARD: USDC is the native gas token AND is exposed as an ERC-20 at 0x3600000000000000000000000000000000000000 backed by the SAME balance (18-dec native view, 6-dec ERC-20 view). address(this).balance and USDC.balanceOf(address(this)) are therefore the same money -- do NOT register that ERC-20 as a stake asset here, and never sum the two views. MEASURED (eth_estimateGas on the live chain): Arc meters code deposit at STANDARD EVM rates -- a 24,576-byte (max EIP-170) contract costs 5,012,361 gas, ~204 gas/byte. The same probe on Tempo costs 25,300,914 gas (~1029 gas/byte), which is why Tempo forced a ~21KB ceiling and facet splitting. Arc therefore needs NO facet splitting: EIP-170's 24,576 bytes is the binding limit, not gas. The per-tx cap is 16,777,216 (2^24, EIP-7825) -- tighter than Tempo's 30M in raw terms, but a max-size deploy uses only ~30% of it. Still simulate FullDeploy without --broadcast and check any BATCHED tx (facet registration + config in one) against the 16.0M ceiling. src/beacon/* is inoperable (EIP-4788 beacon-roots contract omitted); PREVRANDAO is always 0.",
